            "review_title": "Review at Yakiuo Ishikawa Saigon",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nGetting to taste Tsukiji's famous fish yakiniku, right here in HCMC.\nJun 2025 • Couples\nRead that the Vietnamese owners pursued the original Yakiuo's owners by convincing them that they would bring this similar quality and innovative concept - that is, to use sashimi-grade fish for yaki (grill) style. Haven't tried the one in Tsukiji Japan, but it was indeed interesting to witness the chefs in action - as they masterfully sliced through the giant slabs of fresh tuna in the open-concept kitchen - before those slices were beautifully presented to us. \n\nThough their menu tells you how you could grill the fish by yourself, you could also let the waitress do it for you since they'd be more seasoned in getting the fish to the right done-ness. A more relaxing experience with the smoke being further from us.\n\nAs far as authentic omakases goes - personally felt this is one of the best value and underrated omakases since the texture, tenderness and portions of the various cuts of their high quality tuna (chutoro, otoro cuts included!) tasted even better than some wagyu omakases we'd tried in town. The red vinegared rice paired well and overall, the course just left a wonderful lingering taste. Worth visiting again.\n\nDefinitely should reserve ahead of time since they only have a rather limited number of tables and private rooms.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nReserve a table in advance.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten September 24, 2025",
